          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Get rid of all your cards. The last player left holding cards is the loser.',
          gameplay: 'Play is clockwise. The player to the left of the dealer leads any card face-up to start the play pile. On your turn you may either beat the top card (play a higher card of the same suit or one of your own trumps on a different suit) and then play a second card of your choice on top, or pick up cards from the pile (3 if the top is not your trump, 5 if it is your trump but not the ace, or the whole pile if it is the ace of your trump). After a pick-up, the next player must beat the new top card or pick up. If the pile is empty, the next player leads any card. Each player has one assigned trump suit; only your own trumps can beat other suits.',
          keyRules: [
            'Each player has a different trump suit agreed before play.',
            'Before play, players give any sixes to the player who has that suit as trumps.',
            'Beat with higher same suit or your trump; then play a second card.',
            'Cannot or will not beat: pick up 3, 5, or whole pile depending on top card.',
            'Last player holding cards loses and deals the next hand.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Hoard your trumps. If you have the Ace of your suit, it's unbeatable by anyone except... nobody? Actually, if you lead it, someone else might trump it with their trump? No, usually your trump beats their non-trump. Trumps vs Trumps? Usually standard rank.",
          intermediate: "Attack the Trump: Lead the opponent's trump suit to force them to play high trumps or pick up.",
          advanced: 'Memory: Know which high cards of your suit are out. If the King is gone, your Queen is boss.',
          tips: [
            'Your suit is your shield.',
            "Don't waste it on small attacks.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
